('v04','Caching: when it helps and when it hurts','longo','Esse mês','tutorial',NULL,'acme','2026-11-12',4,'{"pairs": [{"title": "Caching: when it helps and when it hurts", "thumb": ""}, {"title": "The cache that took down our API", "thumb": ""}, {"title": "", "thumb": ""}], "thumb_desc": "1: cache diagram in front of the database, big text CACHE\n2: latency chart going up", "hook": {"confirmacao": "Everyone adds a cache when the system gets slow.", "promessa": "Today I''ll show you **when** it fixes things and when it becomes the problem."}, "conteudo": "## The problem\n- the same reads hitting the database\n- high latency at peak\n\n## Strategies\n1. cache-aside\n2. write-through\n3. TTL and invalidation\n\n> A cache is a copy. Every copy can go stale.\n\n- [x] draw the diagram\n- [ ] record the demo", "insercao": "Acme: 45s, after the strategies part.", "conclusao": "Start without a cache, measure, and only then add one."}','{"cortes_ig": false, "shorts": false, "tiktok": false, "linkedin": false, "journal": false}'),
